  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-purple">🔥</span>Flow Stress &amp; Temp</h3>
    <p><strong>Flow Stress:</strong> <code>Y_f = K * ε^n</code> (Stress needed to keep metal deforming).</p>
    <p><strong>Temperatures:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cold:</strong> High force, strain hardening, good finish/tolerance.</li>
      <li><strong>Hot:</strong> Above recrystallization temp. Low force, large shape changes, no strain hardening, scale/poor finish.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="topic-divider"><h3>⚙️ Rolling</h3></div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-green">⚙️</span>Flat Rolling Limits <span class="badge badge-exam">EXAM</span></h3>
    <p>Reducing thickness between 2 opposing rolls.</p>
    <pre>Draft (d) = t_o - t_f
Max Draft (d_max) = μ^2 * R</pre>
    <div class="warn">Friction (μ) limits the draft per pass. To get a bigger draft, you need larger rolls or higher friction (hot rolling).</div>
  </div>

  <div class="topic-divider"><h3>🔨 Forging &amp; Extrusion</h3></div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-red">🔨</span>Forging Types</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Open-die:</strong> Flat dies (bulges/barrels due to friction).</li>
      <li><strong>Impression-die:</strong> Dies contain shape. Excess metal squeezes out as <strong>flash</strong> (which helps build pressure to fill corners).</li>
      <li><strong>Flashless:</strong> Work fully enclosed (coining). Requires exact starting volume.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  
  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-blue">➡️</span>Extrusion</h3>
    <p><strong>Direct:</strong> Ram pushes billet toward die. High friction because billet slides against container wall.</p>
    <p><strong>Indirect:</strong> Die mounted on hollow ram; metal flows backward. No container friction = lower force.</p>
  </div>
