    <p><strong>Blanking:</strong> Cut piece is the part (keep slug). <strong>Punching:</strong> Cut piece is scrap (keep sheet).</p>
    <pre>Clearance (c) = A_c * t</pre>
    <p><em>Sizing rule of thumb:</em> The part takes its size from the tool it is pushed against.</p>
    <ul><li><strong>Blanking:</strong> Die = D_b, Punch = D_b - 2c</li><li><strong>Punching:</strong> Punch = D_h, Die = D_h + 2c</li></ul>
  </div>

  <div class="topic-divider"><h3>📐 Bending</h3></div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-yellow">📐</span>Bend Allowance &amp; Springback</h3>
    <p>Metal outside is stretched, inside is compressed. Neutral axis length stays same.</p>
    <pre>BA = 2π * (α / 360) * (R + K_ba * t)</pre>
    <p><strong>Springback:</strong> Elastic recovery opens the bend. Fix by <strong>overbending</strong> or <strong>bottoming</strong> (coining the bend).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="topic-divider"><h3>🕳️ Deep Drawing</h3></div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3><span class="icon icon-purple">🕳️</span>Drawing Feasibility <span class="badge badge-exam">EXAM</span></h3>
    <p>Forming a flat blank into a hollow shape (cups, cans).</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Drawing Ratio <code>DR = D_b / D_p ≤ 2.0</code></li>
      <li>Reduction <code>r = (D_b - D_p) / D_b ≤ 0.50</code></li>
      <li>Thickness Ratio <code>t / D_b ≥ 1%</code></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="warn">If constraints are exceeded, the part requires <strong>redrawing</strong> steps. Too thin a blank causes <strong>wrinkling</strong>.</div>
  </div>
